A sprawling organic tree viewed from above, its branches forming an intricate radial pattern resembling neural pathways, with the central trunk representing "water" - branches splitting into smaller tributaries that hold tiny detailed vignettes: a raindrop, ocean waves, ice crystals, a river delta, clouds, and a glass being filled. The entire composition rendered in Vincent van Gogh's distinctive post-impressionist style with bold swirling brushstrokes in deep blues, teals, and whites, thick impasto texture creating movement and energy throughout. The branches curve and spiral with Van Gogh's characteristic dynamic flow, connecting each water-themed element in an organic web against a warm golden-yellow background with his signature turbulent sky treatment. The overall effect suggests both natural growth patterns and organized thought, with visible brushwork creating rhythm and visual hierarchy from center to edges.
